    "hor_gyade": {
      "abolition_note": "Directly supervised by the Qing Amban in Lhasa until 1912. The Lhasa Kashag abolished the hereditary Hor Kings (such as Tshewang Tenzin) in 1916 and installed the Horchi commissioner, upgrading this to the Byang-chub Spyi-khyab in 1942; nevertheless, tribal baihu/sheg autonomy and mutual-aid pacts persisted across the 39 Tribes until the 1950-1951 Chamdo-Nagqu PLA integration and Seventeen Point Agreement (1951), with residual tribal structures dissolved in the 1959 democratic reforms.",
      "active_years": [
        1912,
        1951
      ],
      "categories": [
        "tusi"
