    "kumul_khanate": {
      "abolition_note": "Semi-autonomous Uyghur jasagh khanate exempt from the 1884 Xinjiang provincehood reforms; ruled by Shah Maqsud (Maqsud Shah) until his death in May 1930, when Governor Jin Shuren proclaimed gaituguiliu and divided the khanate into Hami, Yiwu, and Yihe counties. Briefly revived in 1931-1932 by Yulbars Khan and Khoja Niyaz behind heir Nasir Shah during the Kumul Rebellion before collapsing into the wider Xinjiang civil war.",
      "active_years": [
        1912,
        1932
      ],
      "categories": [
